->\n            \n      <div class=\"mj-column-per-100 mj-outlook-group-fix\" style=\"font-size:0px;text-align:left;direction:ltr;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;width:100%;\">\n        \n      <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\">\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td style=\"vertical-align:top;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;\">\n              \n    <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"\" width=\"100%\">\n          <tbody>\n            \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"center\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:10px;padding-right:20px;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:20px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <p style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:100%;\">\n      </p>\n      \n      <!--[if mso | IE]><table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:520px;\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"520px\" ><tr><td style=\"height:0;line-height:0;\"> &nbsp;\n</td></tr></table><![endif]-->\n    \n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr>\n                    \n                    \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:12px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:12px;padding-left:24px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <div style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.25;text-align:left;color:#000000;\"><h2 style=\"margin-top: 14pt;margin-bottom: 4pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Buying a Business Just for the Job? Yes, Please.</span></h2><p>Sara,</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Some folks buy businesses the way you\u2019d buy an investment property: polish it up, raise the rates, flip it for more.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Others? They\u2019re just looking for a really, really good job. And guess what? That\u2019s not only okay\u2014it\u2019s smart.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">I see two big groups who should absolutely buy a business with the goal of running it themselves:</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">1. The Relocators</span><br><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\"><strong><br></strong>Moving to small-town America? Trading your city commute for a lake view, golf course, or fly-fishing stream? The problem is, high-paying jobs don\u2019t grow on trees in those zip codes.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">But you know what does exist? That local Main Street accounting firm whose owner is ready to retire. Buy it, and you\u2019re not just getting income; you\u2019re buying your instantaneous ticket into the <em>fabric of the community.</em> That\u2019s priceless.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">2. The \u201cNot-So-Newbies\u201d </span><br><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\"><br>If you\u2019re 22 with no mortgage and zero dependents,  sure, bootstrapping a firm from scratch might work. But if you\u2019ve already built a life (and taken on a mortgage) based on making $150K a year, slow growth isn\u2019t cute.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Buying a firm with an SBA loan means you can step straight into a business that already covers your lifestyle and gives you a platform to grow from. Instead of slogging through 10 years of \u201cgrind,\u201d you start with something that feels like year 11.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">The takeaway? Buying a business isn\u2019t always about \u201cthe exit.\u201d Sometimes it\u2019s about building a life you actually want to live\u2014today.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Curious about whether you\u2019re a \u201crelocator\u201d or a \u201cnot-so-newbie\u201d?</span><br><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\"><br> \ud83d\udc49 </span><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/4c1688ff11c?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn\"><span style=\"color: #3425db !important; color: #3425db !important; font-size: 14px\">Watch the full video on Dealmakers YouTube here.</span></a></p><p style=\"margin-top: 12pt;margin-bottom: 12pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Here\u2019s to building businesses that also build lives,<br>Sara Sharp<br>Partner, SK&amp;S Law Group<br>Founder, Deal Academy</span></p></div>\n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr>\n                    \n                    \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:12px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:12px;padding-left: